# {{ .ProviderShortName }} Provider

The Kinde provider is used to interact with [Kinde Identity Platform](https://kinde.com/) resources. The provider needs to be configured with proper credentials before it can be used.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile "examples/provider/provider.tf" }}

## Required scopes

The provider authenticates as a Kinde machine-to-machine (M2M) application. Authorize that application for the Kinde Management API with the scopes for each resource and data source you use:

| Resource or data source | Scopes |
|---|---|
| `kinde_api` resource | `create:apis`, `read:apis`, `delete:apis` |
| `kinde_api` data source | `read:apis` |
| `kinde_application` resource | `create:applications`, `read:applications`, `update:applications`, `delete:applications`, `read:application_logout_uris`, `read:applications_redirect_uris` |
| `kinde_application` data source | `read:applications` |
| `kinde_application_connection` | `create:application_connections`, `read:application_connections`, `delete:application_connections` |
| `kinde_connection` | `create:connections`, `read:connections`, `update:connections`, `delete:connections` |
| `kinde_connections` data source | `read:connections` |
| `kinde_organization` | `create:organizations`, `read:organizations`, `update:organizations`, `delete:organizations` |
| `kinde_organization_user` | `create:organization_users`, `delete:organization_users`, `create:organization_user_roles`, `read:organization_user_roles`, `delete:organization_user_roles` |
| `kinde_permission` | `create:permissions`, `read:permissions`, `update:permissions`, `delete:permissions` |
| `kinde_role` | `create:roles`, `read:roles`, `update:roles`, `delete:roles`, `read:role_permissions`, `update:role_permissions` |
| `kinde_user` | `create:users`, `read:users`, `update:users`, `delete:users`, `create:user_identities`, `read:user_identities` |
| `kinde_user_role` | `create:organization_user_roles`, `read:organization_user_roles`, `delete:organization_user_roles` |

Kinde spells the redirect URI scope `applications_redirect_uris` and the logout URI scope `application_logout_uris`.

